===Etymology===
{{PIE word|en|dwóh₁}}
From {{inh|en|enm|betwene}}, from {{inh|en|ang|betwēonum|t=between, among|lit=by the two, near both|pos=dative plural}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*bi-|t=be-}} + {{m|gem-pro|*twīhnaz|t=two each}}, corresponding to {{prefix|en|be|twain}}. Cognate with {{cog|sco|between|t=between}}, {{cog|sco|atween|t=between}}, {{cog|got|𐍄𐍅𐌴𐌹𐌷𐌽𐌰𐌹|t=two each}}, {{cog|ang|betweoh|t=between}}, {{cog|ang|twinn|t=double, twofold}}. More at {{l|en|betwixt}}, {{l|en|twin}}.

More distantly related to {{cog|grc|διά||through, across, by, over}} whence {{cog|en|dia-||through, across, between}}.

For the meaning development also compare with {{m+|mn|хооронд||between}}, connected with {{m+|mn|хоёр||two}}.

